        ["Switch.ExamplesTitle"] = "EXAMPLES & BEHAVIOR GUIDE",
        ["Switch.ExamplesBody"] = "1) Two-state ON/OFF switch controlling ONE War Thunder toggle command (Gear, Airbrake, etc.)\r\nON  -> Conditions: 20=ON  | Virtual: 1 | Enter state | Pulse once\r\nOFF -> Conditions: 20=OFF | Virtual: 1 | Enter state | Pulse once\r\nResult: every physical transition taps the same virtual button once, just like pressing the same keyboard key.\r\n\r\n2) Two-state switch with DIFFERENT commands for ON and OFF\r\nON  -> Virtual 1 | Enter state | Pulse once\r\nOFF -> Virtual 2 | Enter state | Pulse once\r\nBind Virtual 1 and Virtual 2 to separate War Thunder commands.\r\n\r\n3) Maintained / held output\r\nON -> Virtual 1 | While active | Hold while active\r\nThe virtual button stays held for as long as that physical state remains active.\r\n\r\n4) Three-state switch\r\nUP / CENTER / DOWN can each have their own conditions and virtual buttons. Use LEARN SWITCH to record all positions automatically.\r\n\r\nWHEN TO ACT\r\nEnter state = fire when moving into this position. Leave state = fire when moving away. While active = evaluate continuously while this position is active. Enter + leave = fire on both edges.\r\n\r\nOUTPUT BEHAVIOR\r\nPulse once = one short virtual-button press. Hold while active = keep the virtual button held. Pulse same command (toggle) = explicit toggle-style pulse behavior for the same command. No output = state is detected but sends nothing.",
